    {
        "content": "<p>I expected to see some definition of area of a geometric object to appear in the statement</p>",
        "id": 626761774,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1790296375
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My understanding is that we're missing a big chunk of general theory on polytopes, but it's also true that there's a lot of extra aliases and whatnot. I'll have it do a simplification pass.</p>",
        "id": 626761806,
        "sender_full_name": "Michal Wallace (tangentstorm)",
        "timestamp": 1790296390
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Okay, the code above indicates that these are trivial algebraic identities and don't actually reflect anything about polytopes. This is certainly not what we would want for the <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/100.html\">100 Theorems</a> site. </p>\n<p>Luckily, there are many smart people working on polyhedral geometry in Mathlib, so hopefully we will have the technology to state these soon!</p>",
        "id": 626762469,
        "sender_full_name": "Jack McCarthy",
        "timestamp": 1790296755
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It seems like this still needs quite a bit of work. I'll keep it running.</p>",
